{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow. Swami targets SwiftUI’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state graph (computed properties, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":") rather than imperative","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"functions, so the two graphs stay aligned. Where a native SwiftUI construct maps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cleanly, Swami uses it. Where Origami’s semantics need a helper — for example the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Interaction patch’s four discrete output ports, or Drag’s momentum + rubber-band"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"physics — Swami ships a helper named after the Origami patch and shaped like it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Corpus-in-progress-2-of-69","level":2,"text":"Corpus (in progress — 2 of 69)","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The translated corpus is the gallery and the training set. Each entry is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"verified SwiftUI translation of an Origami pattern."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Interaction","level":3,"text":"Interaction","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"doc:Interaction_Touch"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_Drag"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Bea